{"Unsafe array access without length check in updateLoadingFrame - accessing request.targets[0].expr without checking if targets array is empty, which violates the established pattern in runSplitGroupedQueries that validates targets.length before accessing array elements": 0.04701419174671173, "Interpolated queries discarded instead of used in query execution - runSplitQuery interpolates queries but passes the original request object with un-interpolated request.targets to runSplitGroupedQueries instead of the interpolated queries array": 0.5486772656440735, "Step calculation uses un-interpolated variables - calculateStep is called with query.step from original metricQueries which may contain un-interpolated variable strings like '$step' instead of resolved values, breaking the fix for issue #107530": 0.09140142053365707, "Interpolating before shard detection loses original query for selector extraction - queries are interpolated via applyTemplateVariables before passing to splitQueriesByStreamShard, causing potential mismatch in groupTargetsByQueryType when queries are grouped by extracted selector string after interpolation": 0.10018545389175415, "Unhandled promise rejection in Observable without error handler - the promise returned by groupTargetsByQueryType is not chained with a .catch() handler, causing potential silent failures leaving UI in loading state": 0.094950832426548, "Interpolated queries in LokiGroupedRequest may be modified by adjustTargetsFromResponseState - targets interpolated early are stored and can be modified in-place during query execution loop, creating stale-data risk on retries and divergence between caller view and actual execution": 0.04504471272230148, "Double interpolation of queries via runSplitQuery and runShardSplitQuery - queries interpolated in runShardSplitQuery are interpolated again inside runSplitQuery, which is inefficient and fragile if interpolation logic changes": 0.49501147866249084}